# language.allow — the three exceptions RULES/43 grants, each with its reason.
#
# The house writes in English. Old Norse — and the runic script its names are carved in — is
# the one other tongue allowed. This file names what is legitimately NOT that, and why. One
# line per entry:
#
#     path | class | reason
#
# class is one of exactly three:
#   fixture    a test that proves unicode handling — the foreign text IS the assertion
#   detector   code that RECOGNISES a foreign language — the words are matching data, and
#              recognising a language is not writing in it
#   quotation  a real person's actual words, kept as spoken, never translated
#
# A reason shorter than a dozen characters is refused, and so is a path that no longer exists:
# a rotten allow line is a lie, and a lie in a gate is worse than no gate.

# ── fixtures: the assertion is the foreign text ──────────────────────────────────
apps/sessrumnir/src/shared/i18n/locales.test.ts | fixture | the locale table's own assertions — every locale string is the test
apps/sessrumnir/src/shared/i18n/pseudo.ts | fixture | the pseudo-locale generator: accented text is the thing it produces
apps/sessrumnir/src/shared/i18n/pseudo.test.ts | fixture | proves the pseudo-locale accents every string it emits
apps/sessrumnir/src/shared/i18n/index.test.ts | fixture | proves the locale resolver against foreign strings
apps/sessrumnir/CONTRIBUTING.md | fixture | quotes the pseudo-locale's own label so a contributor can find it
apps/sessrumnir/src/main/git-worktree.test.ts | fixture | a git error string carrying every accent, as proof it survives a parse
apps/sessrumnir/src/main/file-service.test.ts | fixture | a unicode filename, as proof the file service keeps it intact
.agents/tests/fm-composer-ghost.test.sh | fixture | unicode in a composer buffer, as proof it round-trips
.agents/tests/fm-daemon.test.sh | fixture | unicode through the daemon, as proof it is not mangled

# ── detectors: the foreign words are matching data, not prose ────────────────────
bin/mail/gna_judge.py | detector | the mail classifier's Swedish invoice and meeting words — the classifier reads those languages, it does not write them
systems/skirnir/services/skirnir.py | detector | the assistant's language hint: a Swedish token list that decides whether the mouth answers in his clients' tongue
systems/skirnir/services/walls-test.sh | detector | the test of that language hint, which must contain the Swedish it detects
docs/fixes/agents/2026-10-22-memory-voice-and-the-window.md | detector | the fix note that records why the Swedish hint exists, quoting the sentence it detects

# ── quotations: a person's own words, kept as spoken ────────────────────────────
assets/Ymir.md | quotation | a transcript of the operator's own session, kept as it was spoken — a quotation is never translated

# ── tables: the letters are the subject, not prose ──────────────────────────────
midgard/design-system/runes.md | table | the rune-to-letter transliteration table: each rune beside the letter it stands for
.agents/tests/fm-pr-check-security.test.sh | fixture | a homoglyph URL (dotless i) as the attack the test must refuse

# ── a program's own output, quoted ──────────────────────────────────────────────
docs/fixes/gate/0.1.53-node-test-with-a-directory-is-not-stable-across-majors.md | quotation | it quotes the Node test reporter's output verbatim, mark glyphs and all

# ── specimens: the rule, and the ward, must be able to name what they refuse ─────
RULES/43-two-tongues.md | specimen | the rule names the foreign letters it refuses, so a reader knows what is meant
docs/fixes/gates/2026-11-02-two-tongues-and-the-khmer-rune.md | specimen | the fix note names those letters too, and quotes the Khmer character it found
bin/gates/guards/language-guard.sh | detector | the ward's own stopword lists and planted faults are matching data — the Swedish it detects must be in it
apps/hlidskjalf/scripts/swedish-contract.integration.ts | fixture | the Swedish-contract test: the Swedish strings ARE the assertion
apps/hlidskjalf/tests/swedish-selection.e2e.mjs | fixture | the Swedish selection test: the accented text is the thing being selected
apps/hlidskjalf/tests/voice.e2e.mjs | fixture | the voice test speaks Swedish samples; the Swedish text is the input under test
systems/skirnir/services/test_voice_language.py | fixture | the language-selection test: Swedish speech and its function words are the assertion
apps/hvergelmir/apps/dna-client-tui/tests/render.test.ts | fixture | vendored upstream test proving CJK width handling — the foreign text IS the assertion
